## Testable assertions

Each row is a single, checkable claim about the finished work. Mark how it is
verified: `tier-1` (deterministic — tests/typecheck/lint/build) or `tier-2`
(rubric review). Aim for enough assertions that "done" is unambiguous; a
handful gets rubber-stamped.

| # | Assertion | Verified by | Status |
|---|-----------|-------------|--------|
| A1 | All existing and new tests pass | tier-1 | pending |
| A2 | `typecheck` reports no errors | tier-1 | pending |
| A3 | `lint` reports no errors | tier-1 | pending |
| A4 | Build succeeds | tier-1 | pending |
| A5 | New behavior is covered by meaningful tests (not just smoke) | tier-2 | pending |
| A6 | The change is the simplest design that satisfies A1–A5 | tier-2 | pending |
| A7 | A reviewer unfamiliar with the change can read it without a walkthrough | tier-2 | pending |
| A8 | No dead code, no commented-out code, no duplicated logic introduced | tier-2 | pending |

